      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The debate surrounding trans athletes in sports revolves around two main perspectives: the \"biological sex\" approach and the \"gender identity\" approach. The biological sex approach, supported by some conservative groups, tends to require athletes to compete in their sex assigned at birth. This perspective is often rooted in concerns about fairness and competitive advantage. \n\nIn contrast, the gender identity approach, more commonly advocated by LGBTQ+ organizations and many advocates for trans rights, prioritizes athletes' self-identified gender over their biological sex. Proponents argue this approach promotes inclusivity and opportunities for trans athletes to participate.",
